{ A later unit's routine hides an earlier unit's of its name, whatever
  their parameters, unless it is declared overload, as in Free Pascal
  (P160): ovbn's Half(Double) hides ovan's Half(Integer), so Half(3)
  converts 3; paslang called ovan's. The output is Free Pascal's. }
program ovuse1;

{$mode objfpc}{$H+}

uses ovan, ovbn;

begin
  WriteLn(Half(3), ' ', Half(2.5));
end.

